From: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ask2(T-M6-2 B2): add fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_l2()

Step 1 of 3 for B2's silicon de-risk proof (plans/ASK2-BRIDGE-OFFLOAD-PLAN.md):
a way to actually arm a port's KeyGen scheme to extract the bridge FDB
L2 composite (PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE) toward the CC comparator. Without
this, patch 0206's cc_test install_l2 debugfs command has a tree to
install but no scheme extracting the right bytes for it to ever match
against.

fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_l2(), modeled directly on the existing plain
fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc() (same preamble/error-restore/direct-scheme
tail, copied verbatim): reprograms the port's bound KeyGen scheme's
KGSE_EKFC to 0xe4000000 (KG_SCH_KN_PORT_ID | KG_SCH_KN_MACDST |
KG_SCH_KN_MACSRC | KG_SCH_KN_ETYPE) and grafts it onto the given CC
tree via KGSE_CCBS, exactly like the base attach_cc's IP-tuple case --
just a different EKFC bit combination. No GEC/dual-lane machinery
needed: every L2 field is a hard-parser "known" field with its own
EKFC bit (plan §2 point 1), unlike the VLAN-v6 dual-lane family which
needs GEC for IPv6.

The 0xe4000000 EKFC value is not a guess: it's identical to the live
vendor L2/bridge classification scheme observed on `.106` (scheme 11,
1,225,734 packets, by far the busiest scheme on that board) -- reused
from this project's own oracle read, not re-derived. What is NOT yet
verified is whether the CC comparator on THIS board's silicon actually
reads the bytes this EKFC extracts in the order cc_pack_key_l2() packs
them -- that is plan §8.1's still-open read-only oracle question, the
next step, not resolved by this patch.

fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_cc() needs no changes: it already generically
resets next_engine/cc_base_offset/cc_bits_sel to 0 for any attach_cc
variant (plain/dual/dual_ekfc/l2 alike), matching existing behavior.

Still fully dormant: nothing in-tree calls this function outside its
own declaration. Live arming (actually calling it against a real
sacrificial port) is a separate, deliberate operator action -- not
performed by this patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c
index ae9759f..c1507a7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c
@@ -64,6 +64,21 @@
 #define KG_SCH_KN_IPDST1	0x00080000
 #define KG_SCH_KN_L4PSRC	0x00000004
 #define KG_SCH_KN_L4PDST	0x00000002
+/*
+ * T-M6-2 B2: hard-parser known-field bits for the bridge FDB L2 composite
+ * (PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE). Named here (unlike the existing inline
+ * 0x80000000 literal for PORT_ID elsewhere in this file) because
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_l2() below composes all four together, where
+ * a bare hex constant would be unreadable. Board-confirmed bit positions:
+ * live .106 KeyGen scheme 11 EKFC 0xe4000000 = PORT_ID|MACDST|MACSRC|
+ * ETYPE decomposes to exactly PORT_ID(bit31)|MACDST(bit30)|MACSRC(bit29)|
+ * ETYPE(bit26), matching plans/ASK2-BRIDGE-OFFLOAD-PLAN.md §2 point 1's
+ * documented hard-parser bit positions.
+ */
+#define KG_SCH_KN_PORT_ID	0x80000000
+#define KG_SCH_KN_MACDST	0x40000000
+#define KG_SCH_KN_MACSRC	0x20000000
+#define KG_SCH_KN_ETYPE		0x04000000
 
 /*
  * KG extract-source enumeration that mirrors the silicon-side
@@ -766,6 +781,97 @@ int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc);
 
+/*
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_l2() - like fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc(), but
+ * arms the port's scheme for the T-M6-2 B2 bridge FDB L2 composite
+ * (PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE, matches cc_pack_key_l2()/CC_KEY_SIZE_L2=15)
+ * instead of the plain 14-byte IP-tuple EKFC composite.
+ *
+ * Unlike the VLAN-v6 dual-lane family below, this needs no GEC: every
+ * field in the L2 composite (PORT_ID, MACDST, MACSRC, ETHERTYPE) is a
+ * hard-parser "known" field with its own KGSE_EKFC bit, so a plain
+ * nonzero EKFC composite is sufficient, exactly like the base
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc()'s IP-tuple case -- just a different bit
+ * combination. gec_dual_lane/gec_keep_ekfc stay false/untouched.
+ *
+ * Board-confirmed EKFC value: 0xe4000000 = KG_SCH_KN_PORT_ID |
+ * KG_SCH_KN_MACDST | KG_SCH_KN_MACSRC | KG_SCH_KN_ETYPE, identical to the
+ * live vendor L2/bridge scheme observed on .106 (scheme 11). Composed
+ * from the same F-190 rule fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc()'s own comment
+ * states: the CC walker compares the KeyGen-EXTRACTED composite and
+ * never re-extracts, so this scheme's EKFC must deterministically match
+ * what cc_pack_key_l2() packs -- unverified beyond the aggregate EKFC
+ * value matching the vendor's own working scheme; the actual CC
+ * comparator byte-order/content for THIS specific composite has not
+ * been directly observed on this board (plan §8.1's oracle check is the
+ * next step, not this patch).
+ *
+ * Return: same as fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc().
+ */
+int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_l2(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
+				  u32 cc_group_off)
+{
+	struct fman_keygen *keygen;
+	struct keygen_scheme *slot;
+	struct fman *fman;
+	struct mutex *lock;
+	u32 saved_ccbs, saved_ekfc;
+	u8 saved_engine, id;
+	int err;
+
+	if (!pcd || !cc_group_off)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	if (hw_port_id < 0x08 || hw_port_id >= 0x28)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	fman = fman_pcd_get_fman(pcd);
+	if (!fman || !fman->keygen)
+		return -ENXIO;
+	keygen = fman->keygen;
+	lock = fman_pcd_get_lock(pcd);
+
+	mutex_lock(lock);
+
+	slot = kg_find_port_scheme(keygen, hw_port_id, &id);
+	if (!slot) {
+		mutex_unlock(lock);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
+	saved_engine = slot->next_engine;
+	saved_ccbs   = slot->cc_bits_sel;
+	saved_ekfc   = slot->ekfc;
+
+	slot->next_engine    = 2;
+	slot->cc_base_offset = 0;
+	slot->cc_bits_sel    = cc_group_off;
+	slot->ekfc           = KG_SCH_KN_PORT_ID | KG_SCH_KN_MACDST |
+				KG_SCH_KN_MACSRC | KG_SCH_KN_ETYPE;
+
+	slot->used = false;
+	err = keygen_scheme_setup(keygen, id, true);
+	if (err) {
+		slot->next_engine = saved_engine;
+		slot->cc_bits_sel = saved_ccbs;
+		slot->ekfc        = saved_ekfc;
+		slot->used = false;
+		(void)keygen_scheme_setup(keygen, id, true);
+		mutex_unlock(lock);
+		return err;
+	}
+
+	{
+		struct fman_port *rxport = fman_port_lookup_rx(fman, hw_port_id);
+
+		if (rxport)
+			(void)fman_port_set_kg_direct_scheme(rxport, id);
+	}
+
+	mutex_unlock(lock);
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_l2);
+
 /*
  * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual() - like fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc(),
  * but arms the port's scheme for F-224/F-236 dual-lane GEC extraction
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
index dd4dec7..171b8e3 100644
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -276,6 +276,20 @@ int fman_pcd_kg_attach_cc(struct fman_pcd_kg_scheme *scheme,
 int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
 			       u32 cc_group_off);
 
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_l2() - like fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc(), but
+ * arms the port's scheme for the T-M6-2 B2 bridge FDB L2 composite
+ * (PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE, matches cc_pack_key_l2()/CC_KEY_SIZE_L2) instead
